{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BGQKonSNsQ67c7WaVK2K59","type":"tool_result","content":"     1\t\"\"\"Starter perturbation finder for Bradley-Terry leaderboard stability (t06).\n     2\t\n     3\tThe evaluator calls ``handle(request) -> response`` with finite JSON-compatible dicts.  The\n     4\tcandidate runs isolated (no files, no network, no shared filesystem) and keeps all state in\n     5\tprocess memory.  Every request/response must stay below 64 MiB of UTF-8 JSON.\n     6\t\n     7\tArray encoding (both directions)\n     8\t--------------------------------\n     9\t``{\"dtype\": \"int32\" | \"float32\", \"shape\": [m], \"encoding\": \"base64\", \"byte_order\": \"little\",\n    10\t\"data\": <base64 of the little-endian bytes>}`` -- exactly these five keys.\n    11\t\n    12\tEpisode protocol (one episode per case x seed; the process may be restarted before each reset)\n    13\t-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    14\t1. ``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int>=0}``\n    15\t   Clear ALL state and seed any randomness.  The seed only initialises randomness; it never\n    16\t   identifies the dataset, plane or workload.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}``.\n    17\t2. ``{\"op\": \"load_chunk\", \"case_token\": str, \"chunk_index\": int, \"n_chunks\": int (1..4),\n    18\t   \"row_offset\": int, \"n_rows_total\": int, \"n_players\": int, \"player_a\": int32[m],\n    19\t   \"player_b\": int32[m], \"outcome\": float32[m]}``   (sent n_chunks times, chunk_index 0..n-1)\n    20\t   Row r (global index row_offset + i) is one comparison between players ``player_a[r]`` and\n    21\t   ``player_b[r]`` (ids 0..n_players-1, per-case relabelled); ``outcome`` is 1.0 if player_a\n    22\t   won, 0.0 if player_b won and 0.5 for a tie.  At most 524,288 rows per chunk.  No names,\n    23\t   text, dates, labels or scores are ever sent.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}``.\n    24\t3. ``{\"op\": \"propose\", \"perturbation\": \"drop\" | \"flip\", \"target\": {\"type\": \"top1\"} |\n    25\t   {\"type\": \"topk_set\", \"k\": int}, \"estimator\": {\"model\": \"bradley_terry\", \"ties\": \"half\",\n    26\t   \"ridge\": float, \"tol\": float}, \"max_size\": int, \"deadline_seconds\": float}``\n    27\t   Return a set of global row indices whose removal (\"drop\") or outcome reversal y -> 1-y\n    28\t   (\"flip\"; tie rows are NOT flippable) changes the target of the fixed estimator:\n    29\t     * estimator: maximise sum_r [y_r log s(t_a - t_b) + (1-y_r) log s(t_b - t_a)]\n    30\t       - ridge/2 * ||t||^2 over log-strengths t (float64; s = logistic; ties count as half wins);\n    31\t       the player set is fixed (players keep their ids even if all their rows are dropped);\n    32\t     * top1 changes if some player j != leader has t_j > t_leader + tol after the change;\n    33\t     * topk_set changes if max_{j outside S} t_j > min_{i in S} t_i + tol, S = original top-k.\n    34\t   Response: ``{\"indices\": int32[s]}`` (array encoding above; strictly increasing, unique,\n    35\t   0 <= index < n_rows_total, s <= max_size) plus optional ``\"diagnostics\"``: a dict of at most\n    36\t   32 entries mapping names (``[A-Za-z0-9_-][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,79}``) to finite numbers.  No other\n    37\t   keys are allowed; malformed responses score as failures.  The evaluator independently\n    38\t   re-verifies the set with its own refit; claimed sizes/diagnostics are ignored.  Smaller\n    39\t   verified sets score higher.  Respond before ``deadline_seconds`` (wall clock, measured by\n    40\t   the evaluator from the request); late responses are failures.\n    41\t\n    42\tDeterminism: the same seed and inputs must give the same index set (a replay is checked).\n    43\t\n    44\tThis starter: one-step influence (AMIP-style) ranking of rows by their first-order effect on\n    45\tthe target margin, then the smallest verifying prefix found by exponential + binary search\n    46\twith exact refits.  Deterministic and lightweight.\n    47\t\"\"\"\n    48\timport base64\n    49\timport time\n    50\t\n    51\timport numpy as np\n    52\t\n    53\t_STATE = {}\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef _decode(arr, dtype, expected_len):\n    57\t    if (not isinstance(arr, dict) or arr.get(\"dtype\") != dtype or arr.get(\"encoding\") != \"base64\"\n    58\t            or arr.get(\"byte_order\") != \"little\"):\n    59\t        raise ValueError(\"bad array\")\n    60\t    out = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(arr[\"data\"]), dtype=np.dtype(dtype).newbyteorder(\"<\"))\n    61\t    if out.shape[0] != expected_len or list(arr[\"shape\"]) != [expected_len]:\n    62\t        raise ValueError(\"bad array shape\")\n    63\t    return out\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef _encode_int32(values):\n    67\t    arr = np.ascontiguousarray(np.asarray(values, dtype=\"<i4\"))\n    68\t    return {\"dtype\": \"int32\", \"shape\": [int(arr.shape[0])], \"encoding\": \"base64\",\n    69\t            \"byte_order\": \"little\", \"data\": base64.b64encode(arr.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tdef _pair_stats(p, a, b, y):\n    73\t    idx = a.astype(np.int64) * p + b.astype(np.int64)\n    74\t    cnt = np.bincount(idx, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p).astype(np.float64)\n    75\t    won = np.bincount(idx, weights=y, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n    76\t    lost = np.bincount(idx, weights=1.0 - y, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n    77\t    return won + lost.T, cnt + cnt.T\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef _fit(S, N, ridge, theta0=None, iters=200, gtol=1e-10):\n    81\t    p = S.shape[0]\n    82\t    theta = np.zeros(p) if theta0 is None else theta0.copy()\n    83\t    score = S.sum(axis=1)\n    84\t\n    85\t    def objective(t):\n    86\t        d = t[:, None] - t[None, :]\n    87\t        return -float((S * np.logaddexp(0.0, -d)).sum()) - 0.5 * ridge * float(t @ t)\n    88\t\n    89\t    value = objective(theta)\n    90\t    for _ in range(iters):\n    91\t        d = theta[:, None] - theta[None, :]\n    92\t        prob = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-d))\n    93\t        grad = score - (N * prob).sum(axis=1) - ridge * theta\n    94\t        if float(np.max(np.abs(grad))) < gtol:\n    95\t            break\n    96\t        w = N * prob * (1.0 - prob)\n    97\t        hess = -w\n    98\t        hess[np.diag_indices(p)] += w.sum(axis=1) + ridge\n    99\t        step = np.linalg.solve(hess, grad)\n   100\t        t = 1.0\n   101\t        while True:\n   102\t            cand = theta + t * step\n   103\t            cv = objective(cand)\n   104\t            if cv >= value - 1e-12 * max(1.0, abs(value)) or t < 1e-10:\n   105\t                break\n   106\t            t *= 0.5\n   107\t        theta, value = cand, cv\n   108\t    return theta\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef _neg_hessian(N, theta, ridge):\n   112\t    d = theta[:, None] - theta[None, :]\n   113\t    prob = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-d))\n   114\t    w = N * prob * (1.0 - prob)\n   115\t    hess = -w\n   116\t    hess[np.diag_indices(theta.shape[0])] += w.sum(axis=1) + ridge\n   117\t    return hess\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\tdef _reset(request):\n   121\t    seed = request.get(\"seed\")\n   122\t    if type(seed) is not int or seed < 0:\n   123\t        raise ValueError(\"bad seed\")\n   124\t    _STATE.clear()\n   125\t    _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   126\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef _load_chunk(request):\n   130\t    n_total, n_chunks, chunk = request[\"n_rows_total\"], request[\"n_chunks\"], request[\"chunk_index\"]\n   131\t    if chunk == 0:\n   132\t        _STATE[\"case_token\"] = request[\"case_token\"]\n   133\t        _STATE[\"n\"] = n_total\n   134\t        _STATE[\"p\"] = request[\"n_players\"]\n   135\t        _STATE[\"a\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.int64)\n   136\t        _STATE[\"b\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.int64)\n   137\t        _STATE[\"y\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.float64)\n   138\t        _STATE[\"loaded\"] = set()\n   139\t        _STATE[\"n_chunks\"] = n_chunks\n   140\t    if request[\"case_token\"] != _STATE.get(\"case_token\") or n_total != _STATE[\"n\"]:\n   141\t        raise ValueError(\"inconsistent chunk\")\n   142\t    m = request[\"player_a\"][\"shape\"][0]\n   143\t    lo = request[\"row_offset\"]\n   144\t    _STATE[\"a\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"player_a\"], \"int32\", m)\n   145\t    _STATE[\"b\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"player_b\"], \"int32\", m)\n   146\t    _STATE[\"y\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"outcome\"], \"float32\", m)\n   147\t    _STATE[\"loaded\"].add(chunk)\n   148\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef _propose(request):\n   152\t    started = time.monotonic()\n   153\t    budget = 0.8 * float(request[\"deadline_seconds\"])\n   154\t    if _STATE.get(\"loaded\") != set(range(_STATE.get(\"n_chunks\", -1))):\n   155\t        raise ValueError(\"data not loaded\")\n   156\t    a, b, y, p = _STATE[\"a\"], _STATE[\"b\"], _STATE[\"y\"], _STATE[\"p\"]\n   157\t    ridge, tol = float(request[\"estimator\"][\"ridge\"]), float(request[\"estimator\"][\"tol\"])\n   158\t    drop = request[\"perturbation\"] == \"drop\"\n   159\t    k = 1 if request[\"target\"][\"type\"] == \"top1\" else int(request[\"target\"][\"k\"])\n   160\t    S0, N0 = _pair_stats(p, a, b, y)\n   161\t    theta0 = _fit(S0, N0, ridge)\n   162\t    order = np.argsort(-theta0, kind=\"stable\")\n   163\t    top = np.zeros(p, dtype=bool)\n   164\t    top[order[:k]] = True\n   165\t    leader, challenger = int(order[k - 1]), int(order[k])\n   166\t\n   167\t    def changed(idx):\n   168\t        ia, ib, iy = a[idx], b[idx], y[idx]\n   169\t        lin = ia * p + ib\n   170\t        if drop:\n   171\t            cnt = np.bincount(lin, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p).astype(np.float64)\n   172\t            won = np.bincount(lin, weights=iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   173\t            lost = np.bincount(lin, weights=1.0 - iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   174\t            S, N = S0 - won - lost.T, N0 - cnt - cnt.T\n   175\t        else:\n   176\t            delta = np.bincount(lin, weights=1.0 - 2.0 * iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   177\t            S, N = S0 + delta - delta.T, N0\n   178\t        theta = _fit(np.maximum(S, 0.0), np.maximum(N, 0.0), ridge, theta0)\n   179\t        return float(theta[~top].max()) > float(theta[top].min()) + tol\n   180\t\n   181\t    # One-step influence of each eligible row on the margin t_leader - t_challenger.\n   182\t    c = np.zeros(p)\n   183\t    c[leader], c[challenger] = 1.0, -1.0\n   184\t    v = np.linalg.solve(_neg_hessian(N0, theta0, ridge), c)\n   185\t    elig = np.arange(a.shape[0]) if drop else np.flatnonzero(y != 0.5)\n   186\t    dv = v[a[elig]] - v[b[elig]]\n   187\t    if drop:\n   188\t        resid = y[elig] - 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(theta0[a[elig]] - theta0[b[elig]])))\n   189\t        effect = -resid * dv\n   190\t    else:\n   191\t        effect = (1.0 - 2.0 * y[elig]) * dv\n   192\t    ranked = elig[np.argsort(effect, kind=\"stable\")]\n   193\t    n = min(len(ranked), int(request[\"max_size\"]))\n   194\t    refits = 0\n   195\t    best = None\n   196\t    size, last_fail = 1, 0\n   197\t    while n > 0 and time.monotonic() - started < budget:\n   198\t        refits += 1\n   199\t        if changed(ranked[:size]):\n   200\t            best = size\n   201\t            break\n   202\t        last_fail = size\n   203\t        if size >= n:\n   204\t            break\n   205\t        size = min(2 * size, n)\n   206\t    if best is not None:\n   207\t        lo, hi = last_fail, best\n   208\t        while hi - lo > 1 and time.monotonic() - started < budget:\n   209\t            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n   210\t            refits += 1\n   211\t            if changed(ranked[:mid]):\n   212\t                hi = mid\n   213\t            else:\n   214\t                lo = mid\n   215\t        best = hi\n   216\t    chosen = np.sort(ranked[:best]) if best is not None else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64)\n   217\t    return {\"indices\": _encode_int32(chosen), \"diagnostics\": {\"refits\": float(refits)}}\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\tdef handle(request):\n   221\t    op = request.get(\"op\") if isinstance(request, dict) else None\n   222\t    if op == \"reset\":\n   223\t        return _reset(request)\n   224\t    if op == \"load_chunk\":\n   225\t        return _load_chunk(request)\n   226\t    if op == \"propose\":\n   227\t        return _propose(request)\n   228\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".venv/**\",\n  \"node_modules/**\",\n  \".git/**\",\n  \".mypy_cache/**\",\n  \".pytest_cache/**\",\n  \".ruff_cache/**\",\n  \".tox/**\",\n  \".nox/**\",\n  \"dist/**\",\n  \"build/**\",\n]\ninclude = [\n]\n\n[integration]\nkind = \"generic\"\nnotes = \"\"\nIDENTICAL","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41699338-08fe-4003-85d0-f33b91a46083","uuid":"620a4d34-f3cf-4c7a-9bac-5bbcdb03ef25","timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:52:34.851Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"     1\t\"\"\"Starter perturbation finder for Bradley-Terry leaderboard stability (t06).\n     2\t\n     3\tThe evaluator calls ``handle(request) -> response`` with finite JSON-compatible dicts.  The\n     4\tcandidate runs isolated (no files, no network, no shared filesystem) and keeps all state in\n     5\tprocess memory.  Every request/response must stay below 64 MiB of UTF-8 JSON.\n     6\t\n     7\tArray encoding (both directions)\n     8\t--------------------------------\n     9\t``{\"dtype\": \"int32\" | \"float32\", \"shape\": [m], \"encoding\": \"base64\", \"byte_order\": \"little\",\n    10\t\"data\": <base64 of the little-endian bytes>}`` -- exactly these five keys.\n    11\t\n    12\tEpisode protocol (one episode per case x seed; the process may be restarted before each reset)\n    13\t-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    14\t1. ``{\"op\": \"reset\", \"seed\": int>=0}``\n    15\t   Clear ALL state and seed any randomness.  The seed only initialises randomness; it never\n    16\t   identifies the dataset, plane or workload.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}``.\n    17\t2. ``{\"op\": \"load_chunk\", \"case_token\": str, \"chunk_index\": int, \"n_chunks\": int (1..4),\n    18\t   \"row_offset\": int, \"n_rows_total\": int, \"n_players\": int, \"player_a\": int32[m],\n    19\t   \"player_b\": int32[m], \"outcome\": float32[m]}``   (sent n_chunks times, chunk_index 0..n-1)\n    20\t   Row r (global index row_offset + i) is one comparison between players ``player_a[r]`` and\n    21\t   ``player_b[r]`` (ids 0..n_players-1, per-case relabelled); ``outcome`` is 1.0 if player_a\n    22\t   won, 0.0 if player_b won and 0.5 for a tie.  At most 524,288 rows per chunk.  No names,\n    23\t   text, dates, labels or scores are ever sent.  Response: exactly ``{\"ok\": true}``.\n    24\t3. ``{\"op\": \"propose\", \"perturbation\": \"drop\" | \"flip\", \"target\": {\"type\": \"top1\"} |\n    25\t   {\"type\": \"topk_set\", \"k\": int}, \"estimator\": {\"model\": \"bradley_terry\", \"ties\": \"half\",\n    26\t   \"ridge\": float, \"tol\": float}, \"max_size\": int, \"deadline_seconds\": float}``\n    27\t   Return a set of global row indices whose removal (\"drop\") or outcome reversal y -> 1-y\n    28\t   (\"flip\"; tie rows are NOT flippable) changes the target of the fixed estimator:\n    29\t     * estimator: maximise sum_r [y_r log s(t_a - t_b) + (1-y_r) log s(t_b - t_a)]\n    30\t       - ridge/2 * ||t||^2 over log-strengths t (float64; s = logistic; ties count as half wins);\n    31\t       the player set is fixed (players keep their ids even if all their rows are dropped);\n    32\t     * top1 changes if some player j != leader has t_j > t_leader + tol after the change;\n    33\t     * topk_set changes if max_{j outside S} t_j > min_{i in S} t_i + tol, S = original top-k.\n    34\t   Response: ``{\"indices\": int32[s]}`` (array encoding above; strictly increasing, unique,\n    35\t   0 <= index < n_rows_total, s <= max_size) plus optional ``\"diagnostics\"``: a dict of at most\n    36\t   32 entries mapping names (``[A-Za-z0-9_-][A-Za-z0-9_.-]{0,79}``) to finite numbers.  No other\n    37\t   keys are allowed; malformed responses score as failures.  The evaluator independently\n    38\t   re-verifies the set with its own refit; claimed sizes/diagnostics are ignored.  Smaller\n    39\t   verified sets score higher.  Respond before ``deadline_seconds`` (wall clock, measured by\n    40\t   the evaluator from the request); late responses are failures.\n    41\t\n    42\tDeterminism: the same seed and inputs must give the same index set (a replay is checked).\n    43\t\n    44\tThis starter: one-step influence (AMIP-style) ranking of rows by their first-order effect on\n    45\tthe target margin, then the smallest verifying prefix found by exponential + binary search\n    46\twith exact refits.  Deterministic and lightweight.\n    47\t\"\"\"\n    48\timport base64\n    49\timport time\n    50\t\n    51\timport numpy as np\n    52\t\n    53\t_STATE = {}\n    54\t\n    55\t\n    56\tdef _decode(arr, dtype, expected_len):\n    57\t    if (not isinstance(arr, dict) or arr.get(\"dtype\") != dtype or arr.get(\"encoding\") != \"base64\"\n    58\t            or arr.get(\"byte_order\") != \"little\"):\n    59\t        raise ValueError(\"bad array\")\n    60\t    out = np.frombuffer(base64.b64decode(arr[\"data\"]), dtype=np.dtype(dtype).newbyteorder(\"<\"))\n    61\t    if out.shape[0] != expected_len or list(arr[\"shape\"]) != [expected_len]:\n    62\t        raise ValueError(\"bad array shape\")\n    63\t    return out\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\tdef _encode_int32(values):\n    67\t    arr = np.ascontiguousarray(np.asarray(values, dtype=\"<i4\"))\n    68\t    return {\"dtype\": \"int32\", \"shape\": [int(arr.shape[0])], \"encoding\": \"base64\",\n    69\t            \"byte_order\": \"little\", \"data\": base64.b64encode(arr.tobytes()).decode(\"ascii\")}\n    70\t\n    71\t\n    72\tdef _pair_stats(p, a, b, y):\n    73\t    idx = a.astype(np.int64) * p + b.astype(np.int64)\n    74\t    cnt = np.bincount(idx, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p).astype(np.float64)\n    75\t    won = np.bincount(idx, weights=y, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n    76\t    lost = np.bincount(idx, weights=1.0 - y, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n    77\t    return won + lost.T, cnt + cnt.T\n    78\t\n    79\t\n    80\tdef _fit(S, N, ridge, theta0=None, iters=200, gtol=1e-10):\n    81\t    p = S.shape[0]\n    82\t    theta = np.zeros(p) if theta0 is None else theta0.copy()\n    83\t    score = S.sum(axis=1)\n    84\t\n    85\t    def objective(t):\n    86\t        d = t[:, None] - t[None, :]\n    87\t        return -float((S * np.logaddexp(0.0, -d)).sum()) - 0.5 * ridge * float(t @ t)\n    88\t\n    89\t    value = objective(theta)\n    90\t    for _ in range(iters):\n    91\t        d = theta[:, None] - theta[None, :]\n    92\t        prob = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-d))\n    93\t        grad = score - (N * prob).sum(axis=1) - ridge * theta\n    94\t        if float(np.max(np.abs(grad))) < gtol:\n    95\t            break\n    96\t        w = N * prob * (1.0 - prob)\n    97\t        hess = -w\n    98\t        hess[np.diag_indices(p)] += w.sum(axis=1) + ridge\n    99\t        step = np.linalg.solve(hess, grad)\n   100\t        t = 1.0\n   101\t        while True:\n   102\t            cand = theta + t * step\n   103\t            cv = objective(cand)\n   104\t            if cv >= value - 1e-12 * max(1.0, abs(value)) or t < 1e-10:\n   105\t                break\n   106\t            t *= 0.5\n   107\t        theta, value = cand, cv\n   108\t    return theta\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\tdef _neg_hessian(N, theta, ridge):\n   112\t    d = theta[:, None] - theta[None, :]\n   113\t    prob = 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-d))\n   114\t    w = N * prob * (1.0 - prob)\n   115\t    hess = -w\n   116\t    hess[np.diag_indices(theta.shape[0])] += w.sum(axis=1) + ridge\n   117\t    return hess\n   118\t\n   119\t\n   120\tdef _reset(request):\n   121\t    seed = request.get(\"seed\")\n   122\t    if type(seed) is not int or seed < 0:\n   123\t        raise ValueError(\"bad seed\")\n   124\t    _STATE.clear()\n   125\t    _STATE[\"rng\"] = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n   126\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   127\t\n   128\t\n   129\tdef _load_chunk(request):\n   130\t    n_total, n_chunks, chunk = request[\"n_rows_total\"], request[\"n_chunks\"], request[\"chunk_index\"]\n   131\t    if chunk == 0:\n   132\t        _STATE[\"case_token\"] = request[\"case_token\"]\n   133\t        _STATE[\"n\"] = n_total\n   134\t        _STATE[\"p\"] = request[\"n_players\"]\n   135\t        _STATE[\"a\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.int64)\n   136\t        _STATE[\"b\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.int64)\n   137\t        _STATE[\"y\"] = np.zeros(n_total, dtype=np.float64)\n   138\t        _STATE[\"loaded\"] = set()\n   139\t        _STATE[\"n_chunks\"] = n_chunks\n   140\t    if request[\"case_token\"] != _STATE.get(\"case_token\") or n_total != _STATE[\"n\"]:\n   141\t        raise ValueError(\"inconsistent chunk\")\n   142\t    m = request[\"player_a\"][\"shape\"][0]\n   143\t    lo = request[\"row_offset\"]\n   144\t    _STATE[\"a\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"player_a\"], \"int32\", m)\n   145\t    _STATE[\"b\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"player_b\"], \"int32\", m)\n   146\t    _STATE[\"y\"][lo:lo + m] = _decode(request[\"outcome\"], \"float32\", m)\n   147\t    _STATE[\"loaded\"].add(chunk)\n   148\t    return {\"ok\": True}\n   149\t\n   150\t\n   151\tdef _propose(request):\n   152\t    started = time.monotonic()\n   153\t    budget = 0.8 * float(request[\"deadline_seconds\"])\n   154\t    if _STATE.get(\"loaded\") != set(range(_STATE.get(\"n_chunks\", -1))):\n   155\t        raise ValueError(\"data not loaded\")\n   156\t    a, b, y, p = _STATE[\"a\"], _STATE[\"b\"], _STATE[\"y\"], _STATE[\"p\"]\n   157\t    ridge, tol = float(request[\"estimator\"][\"ridge\"]), float(request[\"estimator\"][\"tol\"])\n   158\t    drop = request[\"perturbation\"] == \"drop\"\n   159\t    k = 1 if request[\"target\"][\"type\"] == \"top1\" else int(request[\"target\"][\"k\"])\n   160\t    S0, N0 = _pair_stats(p, a, b, y)\n   161\t    theta0 = _fit(S0, N0, ridge)\n   162\t    order = np.argsort(-theta0, kind=\"stable\")\n   163\t    top = np.zeros(p, dtype=bool)\n   164\t    top[order[:k]] = True\n   165\t    leader, challenger = int(order[k - 1]), int(order[k])\n   166\t\n   167\t    def changed(idx):\n   168\t        ia, ib, iy = a[idx], b[idx], y[idx]\n   169\t        lin = ia * p + ib\n   170\t        if drop:\n   171\t            cnt = np.bincount(lin, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p).astype(np.float64)\n   172\t            won = np.bincount(lin, weights=iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   173\t            lost = np.bincount(lin, weights=1.0 - iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   174\t            S, N = S0 - won - lost.T, N0 - cnt - cnt.T\n   175\t        else:\n   176\t            delta = np.bincount(lin, weights=1.0 - 2.0 * iy, minlength=p * p).reshape(p, p)\n   177\t            S, N = S0 + delta - delta.T, N0\n   178\t        theta = _fit(np.maximum(S, 0.0), np.maximum(N, 0.0), ridge, theta0)\n   179\t        return float(theta[~top].max()) > float(theta[top].min()) + tol\n   180\t\n   181\t    # One-step influence of each eligible row on the margin t_leader - t_challenger.\n   182\t    c = np.zeros(p)\n   183\t    c[leader], c[challenger] = 1.0, -1.0\n   184\t    v = np.linalg.solve(_neg_hessian(N0, theta0, ridge), c)\n   185\t    elig = np.arange(a.shape[0]) if drop else np.flatnonzero(y != 0.5)\n   186\t    dv = v[a[elig]] - v[b[elig]]\n   187\t    if drop:\n   188\t        resid = y[elig] - 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-(theta0[a[elig]] - theta0[b[elig]])))\n   189\t        effect = -resid * dv\n   190\t    else:\n   191\t        effect = (1.0 - 2.0 * y[elig]) * dv\n   192\t    ranked = elig[np.argsort(effect, kind=\"stable\")]\n   193\t    n = min(len(ranked), int(request[\"max_size\"]))\n   194\t    refits = 0\n   195\t    best = None\n   196\t    size, last_fail = 1, 0\n   197\t    while n > 0 and time.monotonic() - started < budget:\n   198\t        refits += 1\n   199\t        if changed(ranked[:size]):\n   200\t            best = size\n   201\t            break\n   202\t        last_fail = size\n   203\t        if size >= n:\n   204\t            break\n   205\t        size = min(2 * size, n)\n   206\t    if best is not None:\n   207\t        lo, hi = last_fail, best\n   208\t        while hi - lo > 1 and time.monotonic() - started < budget:\n   209\t            mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n   210\t            refits += 1\n   211\t            if changed(ranked[:mid]):\n   212\t                hi = mid\n   213\t            else:\n   214\t                lo = mid\n   215\t        best = hi\n   216\t    chosen = np.sort(ranked[:best]) if best is not None else np.zeros(0, dtype=np.int64)\n   217\t    return {\"indices\": _encode_int32(chosen), \"diagnostics\": {\"refits\": float(refits)}}\n   218\t\n   219\t\n   220\tdef handle(request):\n   221\t    op = request.get(\"op\") if isinstance(request, dict) else None\n   222\t    if op == \"reset\":\n   223\t        return _reset(request)\n   224\t    if op == \"load_chunk\":\n   225\t        return _load_chunk(request)\n   226\t    if op == \"propose\":\n   227\t        return _propose(request)\n   228\t    raise ValueError(\"unknown op\")\nschema_version = 1\ncode_root = \"src\"\n\n[entrypoint]\npath = \"program.py\"\nlanguage = \"python\"\ntype = \"script\"\n\n[copy]\nexclude = [\n  \"**/__pycache__/**\",\n  \"**/*.pyc\",\n  \".