{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hds7AewPqXAM4DedBmtoXR","type":"tool_result","content":"- schemas/verification-report.schema.json\n- bundle.manifest.json\n- ledger.jsonl\nbundle.manifest.json\nledger.jsonl\nschemas\nspec.md\n# scientific-evidence\n\nThis is the canonical generated spec bundle for the `scientific-evidence` skill.\nUse the skill script as the source of truth for schemas, layout, and wording.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis contract is generic and file-format-agnostic.\nIt supports inline evidence refs in text-like files, adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts, and a central JSONL ledger.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe point of `scientific-evidence` is to make an agent leave a machine-checkable trail for important numbers, figures, tables, and derived outputs.\nA paper or report should not depend on free-form prose alone when those claims can point back to real artifacts.\nAlways use this contract during paper writing whenever the agent adds manuscript numbers, table values, figure inputs, or derived statistics.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\nAgents should use this layout exactly. Do not invent alternate bundle directories.\n\n## Grammar\n\n```text\nEvidenceRef   := '@evidence[[' Target [ '#' Locator ] ']]'\nTarget        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\nLocator       := opaque fragment without closing ']]'\nSidecar       := '<artifact>.prov.json'\nLedger        := 'scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl'\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Target` stays generic. The verifier may classify it as `path`, `absolute-path`, `uri`, `id`, or `unknown`.\n- `Locator` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Text-like artifacts should use inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs. Binary or generated outputs should carry an adjacent `.prov.json` sidecar.\n\n### Minimal examples\n\n- `@evidence[[TARGET]]`\n- `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `figure.png.prov.json`\n\n## Verification behavior\n\nA verifier uses this bundle to inspect whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\nThe base verifier uses three reference states:\n\n- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\n- `dangling`: the target does not resolve, the sidecar chain breaks, or the reference is malformed.\n\n### Minimum verifier expectations\n\n1. Resolve every inline evidence ref to a target path, URI, or id when possible.\n2. Mark each ref as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`.\n3. For manifests, require every `derived_from` edge to resolve to at least `anchored`.\n4. When hashes are recorded, compare them. Missing hashes are allowed.\n5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\n\n### What verification should prove\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n\n- scan text-like artifacts for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41699338-08fe-4003-85d0-f33b91a46083","uuid":"ef8dfbf3-4f45-4070-b6d2-78857146cd09","timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:58:35.722Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- schemas/verification-report.schema.json\n- bundle.manifest.json\n- ledger.jsonl\nbundle.manifest.json\nledger.jsonl\nschemas\nspec.md\n# scientific-evidence\n\nThis is the canonical generated spec bundle for the `scientific-evidence` skill.\nUse the skill script as the source of truth for schemas, layout, and wording.\n\n## Scope\n\nThis contract is generic and file-format-agnostic.\nIt supports inline evidence refs in text-like files, adjacent `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts, and a central JSONL ledger.\n\n## Why this exists\n\nThe point of `scientific-evidence` is to make an agent leave a machine-checkable trail for important numbers, figures, tables, and derived outputs.\nA paper or report should not depend on free-form prose alone when those claims can point back to real artifacts.\nAlways use this contract during paper writing whenever the agent adds manuscript numbers, table values, figure inputs, or derived statistics.\n\n## Fixed directory structure\n\n```text\nscientific-evidence/\n  spec.md\n  bundle.manifest.json\n  ledger.jsonl\n  schemas/\n    evidence-reference.schema.json\n    artifact-manifest.schema.json\n    ledger-entry.schema.json\n    verification-report.schema.json\n```\n\nAgents should use this layout exactly. Do not invent alternate bundle directories.\n\n## Grammar\n\n```text\nEvidenceRef   := '@evidence[[' Target [ '#' Locator ] ']]'\nTarget        := non-empty path | absolute path | URI | stable identifier\nLocator       := opaque fragment without closing ']]'\nSidecar       := '<artifact>.prov.json'\nLedger        := 'scientific-evidence/ledger.jsonl'\n```\n\n### Notes\n\n- `Target` stays generic. The verifier may classify it as `path`, `absolute-path`, `uri`, `id`, or `unknown`.\n- `Locator` is opaque unless a verifier adapter knows how to interpret it.\n- Text-like artifacts should use inline `@evidence[[...]]` refs. Binary or generated outputs should carry an adjacent `.prov.json` sidecar.\n\n### Minimal examples\n\n- `@evidence[[TARGET]]`\n- `@evidence[[TARGET#LOCATOR]]`\n- `figure.png.prov.json`\n\n## Verification behavior\n\nA verifier uses this bundle to inspect whether the agent left a connected evidence trail.\nThe base verifier uses three reference states:\n\n- `resolved`: the target exists and the verifier can validate the locator semantics it understands.\n- `anchored`: the target exists, but only path/hash checks were possible or the locator remained opaque.\n- `dangling`: the target does not resolve, the sidecar chain breaks, or the reference is malformed.\n\n### Minimum verifier expectations\n\n1. Resolve every inline evidence ref to a target path, URI, or id when possible.\n2. Mark each ref as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`.\n3. For manifests, require every `derived_from` edge to resolve to at least `anchored`.\n4. When hashes are recorded, compare them. Missing hashes are allowed.\n5. Do not pretend to interpret unknown locator grammars. Keep them `anchored` unless an adapter proves more.\n\n### What verification should prove\n\nAt a minimum, a downstream verifier should be able to:\n\n- scan text-like artifacts for `@evidence[[...]]` refs\n- read `.prov.json` sidecars for generated artifacts\n- resolve refs against real files or stable ids\n- classify each link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`\n- fail when a generated artifact has no input trail or when a claimed source does not exist","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVYRatSAm2AvKYzSn6ZM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017aViXg2VmE1529cQtQQ3cB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"mkdir -p /workspace/paper/analysis && cat > /workspace/paper/analysis/derive_stats.py <<'PY'\n\"\"\"Derive per-case statistics for the paper from the sealed final evaluation record.\n\nEvery number is read from paper_data.json (final_evaluation); nothing is hardcoded.\nOutputs analysis/derived_stats.json (+ .prov.json sidecar).\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]]\ndata = json.loads((ROOT / \"paper_data.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\nfinal = data[\"final_evaluation\"]\nmetrics = final[\"metrics\"]\nepisodes = final[\"evaluation_evidence\"][\"episodes\"]\n\n# Verified sizes must be identical across seeds (determinism); keep seed-level record.\nper_seed = {int(ep[\"seed\"]): ep[\"solution\"][\"verified_k\"] for ep in episodes}\nseeds = sorted(per_seed)\ncase_ids = sorted(per_seed[seeds[0]])\nidentical = all(per_seed[s] == per_seed[seeds[0]] for s in seeds)\nk = per_seed[seeds[0]]\n\n# Row counts n per source, derived exactly from k and the evaluator-reported fraction k/n.\n# Single-source families: n = k_drop_top1 / top1_drop_frac.\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.arena140k_top1_drop_frac]]\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.mtbench_human_top1_drop_frac]]\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.mtbench_gpt4_top1_drop_frac]]\nn = {}\nfor fam in (\"arena140k\", \"mtbench_human\", \"mtbench_gpt4\"):\n    n[fam] = k[f\"{fam}_drop_top1\"] / metrics[f\"{fam}_top1_drop_frac\"]\n# NBA family reports the mean fraction over two seasons for drop and for flip:\n#   (kd14/n14 + kd15/n15)/2 = Fd,  (kf14/n14 + kf15/n15)/2 = Ff  -> solve 2x2 linear system in 1/n.\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.nba_top1_drop_frac]]\n# @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics.nba_top1_flip_frac]]\na11, a12, r1 = k[\"nba2014_drop_top1\"], k[\"nba2015_drop_top1\"], 2 * metrics[\"nba_top1_drop_frac\"]\na21, a22, r2 = k[\"nba2014_flip_top1\"], k[\"nba2015_flip_top1\"], 2 * metrics[\"nba_top1_flip_frac\"]\ndet = a11 * a22 - a12 * a21\ninv14 = (r1 * a22 - a12 * r2) / det\ninv15 = (a11 * r2 - r1 * a21) / det\nn[\"nba2014\"], n[\"nba2015\"] = 1.0 / inv14, 1.0 / inv15\nn_int = {s: int(round(v)) for s, v in n.items()}\n\nSOURCES = [\"arena140k\", \"mtbench_human\", \"mtbench_gpt4\", \"nba2014\", \"nba2015\"]\nTOPK = {\"arena140k\": 5, \"mtbench_human\": 3, \"mtbench_gpt4\": 3, \"nba2014\": 5, \"nba2015\": 5}\ncases = []\nfor src in SOURCES:\n    for pert, tgt in ((\"drop\", \"top1\"), (\"flip\", \"top1\"), (\"drop\", f\"top{TOPK[src]}\")):\n        cid = f\"{src}_{pert}_{tgt}\"\n        kv = k[cid]\n        cases.append({\"case\": cid, \"source\": src, \"perturbation\": pert, \"target\": tgt,\n                      \"k\": kv, \"n\": n_int[src], \"frac_pct\": 100.0 * kv / n_int[src]})\n\nratios = {src: k[f\"{src}_drop_top1\"] / k[f\"{src}_flip_top1\"] for src in SOURCES}\ntopk_over_top1 = {src: k[f\"{src}_drop_top{TOPK[src]}\"] / k[f\"{src}_drop_top1\"] for src in SOURCES}\n\nout = {\n    \"seeds\": seeds,\n    \"verified_k_identical_across_seeds\": identical,\n    \"episode_durations_seconds\": {int(ep[\"seed\"]): ep[\"duration_seconds\"] for ep in episodes},\n    \"n_rows_derived\": n_int,\n    \"n_rows_derived_unrounded\": n,\n    \"cases\": cases,\n    \"drop_over_flip_top1\": ratios,\n    \"topk_over_top1_drop\": topk_over_top1,\n    \"controls\": {\"synthetic_drop_top1_k\": k[\"synthetic_drop_top1\"],\n                 \"synthetic_control_score\": metrics[\"synthetic_control_score\"],\n                 \"perm_arena140k_drop_top1_k\": k[\"perm_arena140k_drop_top1\"],\n                 \"permutation_control_score\": metrics[\"permutation_control_score\"]},\n    \"comparators\": {key: metrics[key] for key in metrics if key.startswith(\"mean_log2_ratio\")},\n    \"random_ratio_x\": 2.0 ** metrics[\"mean_log2_ratio_vs_random\"],\n    \"random_ratio_ci_x\": [2.0 ** metrics[\"mean_log2_ratio_vs_random_ci_low\"],\n                          2.0 ** metrics[\"mean_log2_ratio_vs_random_ci_high\"]],\n    \"nba_mean_drop_frac_pct\": 100 * metrics[\"nba_top1_drop_frac\"],\n    \"nba_mean_flip_frac_pct\": 100 * metrics[\"nba_top1_flip_frac\"],\n}\ndst = ROOT / \"analysis\" / \"derived_stats.json\"\ndst.write_text(json.dumps(out, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n(ROOT / \"analysis\" / \"derived_stats.json.prov.json\").write_text(json.dumps({\n    \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n    \"artifact\": {\"path\": \"analysis/derived_stats.json\", \"kind\": \"derived-data\"},\n    \"derived_from\": [\"@evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation]]\",\n                     \"@evidence[[analysis/derive_stats.py]]\"],\n}, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\nprint(json.dumps(out, indent=1))\nPY\ncd /workspace/paper && python3 analysis/derive_stats.py","description":"Write and run derivation script for per-case stats"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1483,"cache_read_input_tokens":124668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1483},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"41699338-08fe-4003-85d0-f33b91a46083","uuid":"2cb162f1-8a33-4350-a5df-dc52caa801a5","timestamp":"2026-10-28T23:58:54.564Z","request_id":"req_011CgVYRZz7UNhBsPw2Ruqjb"}
